    │   libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt is used here as a synchronous, callback-based MQTT client to connect and publish sensor readings. aiomqtt, gmqtt, and amqtt are all MQTT 
        client libraries capable of connecting to a broker and publishing messages, making them functionally equivalent at the protocol/purpose level (MQTT 
        pub/sub client). However, they use async/await and context-manager based connection lifecycles instead of paho's synchronous connect()/publish() calls.

