│    37     paho-mqtt's `Client.connect()`/`.publish()`/`.disconnect()` are plain                                                                             │
│    38     blocking calls, and the `Client` instance keeps its socket/session state                                                                          │
│    39     alive across many calls. amqtt only exposes coroutines                                                                                            │
│    40     (`MQTTClient.connect()`, `.publish()`, `.disconnect()`), so this facade                                                                           │
